summary:
- topic: Administrator Contract Ratified
  text: The board unanimously ratified a new three-year collective bargaining agreement
    (2025-2028) with the South Portland Administrators Association following an executive
    session.
- topic: New School Year Preparations
  text: Student Representative Angela Kabisa provided updates from various schools
    preparing for the new year, including new staff, building upgrades, and schedule
    changes at the high school.
- topic: High School Cell Phone Policy
  text: A report on a stricter cell phone practice at the high school prompted a board
    discussion about the difference between administrative practices and board-level
    policy, with members requesting more information and considering a future policy
    review.
- topic: Financial Deficit Update
  text: The Finance Committee reported a projected FY25 budget deficit of approximately
    $1.6 million. The new Director of Finance is analyzing the situation, awaiting
    a mid-September audit for clearer figures, and exploring solutions including creating
    an educational foundation for fundraising.
- topic: Vice Chair Election
  text: Following nominations and debate, the board elected Ms. DeAngelis as the new
    Vice Chair in a 4-2 ballot vote against Ms. Holman. Discussion centered on board
    leadership precedent and the need for stability amid upcoming board member turnover.
- topic: Athletic Field Referendum Language
  text: The board approved revised wording for the upcoming municipal referendum on
    the middle school athletic field. The changes clarify the choice between a "natural
    grass" field and a "synthetic turf" field to prevent voter confusion.
- topic: Leadership Transitions
  text: The board formally welcomed Interim Superintendent George Entwistle. Chair
    Ratliff also announced she would not be seeking re-election for her District 2
    seat as she will be moving at the end of her term.
